OpenSSL 4.1.0: ECH with a HelloRetryRequest fails when the client sends a custom extension of its own

Upstream code: the ssl/statem/extensions.c hunk of OpenSSL commit openssl/openssl@981f976bb0 (PR #33246, issue #33231), verbatim, as
merged to master, openssl-4.1 and openssl-4.0 on 2026-11-13. Its test hunks (test/ech_test.c, test/quicapitest.c) are
omitted: the bundled build is configured with no-tests. Carried by Kuicksilver under ADR-0019
(docs/adr/0019-openssl-4-and-ech.md); pinned by its SHA-256 in gradle/openssl.toml, applied by tools/openssl/apply-patch.pl
to the verified tarball, and dropped with OpenSSL 4.1.1, the first release that has the commit.

The bug: tls_construct_extensions resets the SENT and RECEIVED flags of the custom extensions (custom_ext_init) at the
start of a ClientHello only when ECH is not attempted. With ECH the second inner ClientHello after a HelloRetryRequest
adds the custom extensions again with their SENT flag still set from the first one, custom_ext_add fails its assertion
that the flag is clear, and the handshake ends with internal_error. QUIC always registers one (quic_transport_parameters),
so every ECH handshake over QUIC that meets a HelloRetryRequest fails. The fix resets the flags at the start of every
inner ClientHello (ch_depth 1).

diff --git a/ssl/statem/extensions.c b/ssl/statem/extensions.c
index be2d52bb085f7..87779b3eb3f70 100644
--- a/ssl/statem/extensions.c
+++ b/ssl/statem/extensions.c
@@ -1187,7 +1187,14 @@ int tls_construct_extensions(SSL_CONNECTION *s, WPACKET *pkt,
 
     /* Add custom extensions first */
 #ifndef OPENSSL_NO_ECH
-    if ((context & SSL_EXT_CLIENT_HELLO) != 0 && s->ext.ech.attempted == 0)
+    /*
+     * With ECH, the outer ClientHello reuses the custom extensions added
+     * to the inner one, so only reset their flags for the inner. That has
+     * to happen for every inner, as after a HelloRetryRequest the flags
+     * would still be set from the first ClientHello.
+     */
+    if ((context & SSL_EXT_CLIENT_HELLO) != 0
+        && (s->ext.ech.attempted == 0 || s->ext.ech.ch_depth == 1))
         /* On the server side with initialise during ClientHello parsing */
         custom_ext_init(&s->cert->custext);
 #else
